# What is NOT uploaded when deploying.
#
# The rule is: source and lockfile go up, everything derived or private stays here.
# Two entries matter more than the rest.
#
#   .env      — real credentials. They belong in the platform's own encrypted store,
#               never in a deployment's file list.
#   .vercel   — local build output. The platform treats a `.vercel/output` directory
#               in an upload as a finished build and skips building. Uploading a
#               stale one would silently deploy yesterday's code.

node_modules
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.vercel
.next
dist
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
*.log

# Generated at install time by the postinstall hook, from prisma/schema.prisma.
packages/db/src/generated

# Test and CI material: nothing here is served or imported by the app.
e2e
playwright-report
test-results
eval/report.json

# Container build files — a different deployment target entirely.
Dockerfile.api
Dockerfile.web
docker-compose.yml

.git
.DS_Store
